  "worked_solution": "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol\n\n$$\nn\\in Z,\\,-1\\le n\\le 2\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any integer number that satisfies the inequality $-1\\le n\\le 2.$ In other words, \n\n$$\nn={-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elements of $B$ are all the terms of the sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{n},\\,n\\in {-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ {b}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{0}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{1}{2},2,8}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
